---
title: German Verification Act (Nachweisgesetz - NachwG Compliance Rules)
sourceType: statutory_statute
date: 2025-06-10
jurisdiction: Germany
language: en
register: statutory_legal
format: docx
---

Employers must provide the essential terms of the employment contract to the employee in writing with a wet-ink signature no later than on the first day of work.

Electronic form pursuant to Section 126a of the German Civil Code (such as DocuSign or Adobe Sign) remains expressly excluded for the primary verification documentation under the Nachweisgesetz.

Non-compliance with the statutory documentation deadlines may be sanctioned as an administrative offense with fines up to €2,000 per violation.
